 "_comment": "Where an Ops Agent metric (agent.googleapis.com/...) comes from in a plain OpenTelemetry Collector and what it is called in New Relic. status VERIFIED = read in the cited source (docs/research/gcp-metric-name-mapping.md); UNVERIFIED = our reading, the Google name is kept in the query. factor: the Google value equals the OpenTelemetry value times factor, so a Google threshold is divided by it. labels: Google label -> OpenTelemetry attribute. drop: label filters that have no equivalent (removed when they match). add: attribute filters the split into Google metrics needs.",
 "agent": {
  "agent.googleapis.com/cpu/utilization": {
   "name": "system.cpu.utilization",
   "status": "VERIFIED",
   "factor": 100,
   "labels": {
    "cpu_state": "state",
