  "agent.googleapis.com/disk/percent_used": {
   "name": "system.filesystem.utilization",
   "status": "VERIFIED",
   "factor": 100,
   "labels": {},
   "drop": [
    {
     "key": "state",
     "value": "used"
    }
   ],
   "add": [],
   "nr_type": "gauge",
   "unit": "1 (ratio)",
   "sources": [
    "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/ops-agent/master/apps/hostmetrics.go",
    "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/opentelemetry-operations-collector/master/components/otelopscol/processor/agentmetricsprocessor/utils_calculate_utilizations.go",
    "https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector-contrib/blob/main/receiver/hostmetricsreceiver/internal/scraper/filesystemscraper/documentation.md"
   ],
   "note": "optional metric of the hostmetrics filesystem scraper: enable it. It has no `state` attribute (it is the used fraction), so a filter state = used is dropped; Google keeps the highest value over the mount points of a device (use max()). Google reports percent (0-100); the OpenTelemetry metric is a ratio (0-1), so a Google threshold is divided by 100."
  },
